{
  "description": "issue #764, review-gate regression: an event emitted inside the per-turtle stamping window is not automatically the acting turtle's, so it is not safe to label with whichever turtle is currently acting. A `clear` is never labelled at all — it describes the shared drawing surface rather than any turtle (spec/turtles-and-sprites.md:113; spec/execution-model.md:998 — `turtle-id` is \"present only when the event is turtle-specific, otherwise absent\") — and `clean` in particular concerns no turtle even semantically, since it only wipes the retained scene and homes nobody. Here `forward wipe` applies once per addressed turtle (spec/turtles-and-sprites.md:113) and evaluates the `wipe` reporter inside each run, so both `clean` events are produced inside the window where the runtime stamps the acting turtle's identity — and both must come out with NO `turtle_id`, rather than being labelled turtle 1 and turtle 2. The two `move`/`draw-segment` pairs the command itself produces do carry their acting turtle's id, and the reporter's own `procedure-enter`/`instruction`/`return`/`procedure-exit` events carry none, being program events.",
